# Third-party licenses

Go modules compiled into the Guard Spec binaries (including the `onnx` build),
as found by [go-licenses](https://github.com/google/go-licenses). Generated by
`make licenses`; do not edit by hand. Native libraries and bundled data are
listed in [NOTICE](NOTICE).

The GPU image (`guard-spec-gateway:<version>-gpu`, an option; the CPU image is
the default) also contains, from its `nvidia/cuda` base image, NVIDIA's CUDA
12 runtime libraries (cudart, cuBLAS, cuFFT, cuRAND and others) under the
[NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit EULA](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/index.html) and
cuDNN 9 under the [NVIDIA cuDNN Software License Agreement](https://docs.nvidia.com/deeplearning/cudnn/latest/reference/eula.html),
which allow redistributing these runtime libraries with an application, and
ONNX Runtime's GPU build (MIT; its third-party notices ship at
`/usr/share/doc/onnxruntime/ThirdPartyNotices.txt`). See NOTICE.

